92186128089}] :question/id #uuid "461f90fa-99b0-5fee-bcc1-f1621ef2267d" :question/math-academy-id "q-40977" :question/problem "What is the minimum value of $f(x) =-\\cos (x + \\frac{π}{4}) + 3$?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233683 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5696c2d5-4e35-5ed3-a4a2-6fe9b158e461" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Range of a Transformed Sinusoidal Function"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "efc3b489-6805-58cd-9ffd-9dce88f3406c" :question/math-academy-id "q-25512" :question/problem "Find the range of the function $f(x)=-2\\operatorname{sin}(3x)+1.$" :question/worked-solution "The range of $\\operatorname{sin}x$ is\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}x\\le 1.\n$$\n\nHorizontal shifts and stretches have no effect on the range. Therefore,\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}(3x)\\le 1.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $-2$ and then adding $1$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & -1\\le \\operatorname{sin}(3x)\\le 1 \\\\  & 2\\ge -2\\operatorname{sin}(2x)\\ge -2 \\\\  & 3\\ge -2\\operatorname{sin}(2x)+1\\ge -1 \\\\  & -1\\le f(x)\\le 3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range is $f(x)\\in [-1,3].$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234034 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5696c2d5-4e35-5ed3-a4a2-6fe9b158e461" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Range of a Transformed Sinusoidal Function"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "35cc2bef-7c45-5174-b681-8a4353622923" :question/math-academy-id "q-40908" :question/problem "What is the range of the function $f(x)=4\\operatorname{sin}(x+{30}^{∘})-2?$" :question/worked-solution "The range of $\\operatorname{sin}x$ is\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}x\\le 1.\n$$\n\nHorizontal shifts and stretches have no effect on the range. Therefore,\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}(x+{30}^{∘})\\le 1.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $4$ and then subtracting $2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & -1\\le \\operatorname{sin}(x+{30}^{∘})\\le 1 \\\\  & -4\\le 4\\operatorname{sin}(x+{30}^{∘})\\le 4 \\\\  & -6\\le 4\\operatorname{sin}(x+{30}^{∘})-2\\le 2 \\\\  & -6\\le f(x)\\le 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range is $f(x)\\in [-6,2].$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186238052 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5696c2d5-4e35-5ed3-a4a2-6fe9b158e461" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Range of a Transformed Sinusoidal Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2bee8a09-1b10-5d3b-a3e0-53f487269fbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\in (-4,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236092} {:answer/id #uuid "3ae5f17b-6d77-50aa-9f3e-7b11978d9ef3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\in [-4,0]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236187} {:answer/id #uuid "6e51c3bd-ccb5-5657-a12f-be75f9b7421d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\in (-4,0]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236517} {:answer/id #uuid "8af5fbbe-fd48-522b-bd11-fcef14c27e77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\in [-4,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236685} {:answer/id #uuid "c5deb01d-4513-5f86-8831-7f209ca52bc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237069}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ae5f17b-6d77-50aa-9f3e-7b11978d9ef3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\in [-4,0]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236187} :answer-field/id #uuid "823dc40d-4f4d-5208-b833-113087963ad8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237612}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9b3308de-6d92-5bb6-a7a9-50e3ea31e7e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-10379" :question/problem "Find the range of the function $y=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)-2.$" :question/worked-solution "The range of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ is\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\le 1.\n$$\n\nHorizontal shifts and stretches have no effect on the range. Therefore,\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\\le 1.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $2$ and then subtracting $2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & -1\\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\\le 1 \\\\  & -2\\le 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\\le 2 \\\\  & -4\\le 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)-2\\le 0 \\\\  & -4\\le y\\le 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range is $y\\in [-4,0].$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326892 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5696c2d5-4e35-5ed3-a4a2-6fe9b158e461" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Range of a Transformed Sinusoidal Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46dbfb94-8f7e-52b5-a0bc-216cfa3f3688" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)\\in [-1,5]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324540} {:answer/id #uuid "761814c1-8f36-5a1f-a9c3-df54f177de2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)\\in [-6,1]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324952} {:answer/id #uuid "8d0d2ae8-7e42-557f-930a-2314bd90d992" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)\\in [0,4]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325169} {:answer/id #uuid "b06eafb2-11d2-56a5-ab67-ec95fe6b25ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)\\in [-3,3]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325476} {:answer/id #uuid "b37f5dc8-1fd1-5b76-b5e2-0cd483be88a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)\\in [-4,0]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325510}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46dbfb94-8f7e-52b5-a0bc-216cfa3f3688" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)\\in [-1,5]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324540} :answer-field/id #uuid "19ba0b8e-1c6b-5fd4-a9f9-80b8a5cf11c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326269}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9d95e69c-d8b6-504a-9a9e-0e0569042175" :question/math-academy-id "q-40903" :question/problem "What is the range of $f(x)=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})+2?$" :question/worked-solution "The range of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ is\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\le 1.\n$$\n\nHorizontal shifts and stretches have no effect on the range. Therefore,\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\le 1.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $3$ and then adding $2$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & -1\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\le 1 \\\\  & -3\\le 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\le 3 \\\\  & -1\\le 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})+2\\le 5 \\\\  & -1\\le f(x)\\le 5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range is $f(x)\\in [-1,5].$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326912 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5696c2d5-4e35-5ed3-a4a2-6fe9b158e461" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Range of a Transformed Sinusoidal Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d1c4191-fab1-56ef-9a9e-5df4f5a37573" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\in [4,6]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324871} {:answer/id #uuid "705447cb-ac85-5790-aadf-544a4a2ca55d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\in [-2,6]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324896} {:answer/id #uuid "c37b50d3-93b0-5e4b-a2f6-ad5ca8b620b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\in [3,6]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325652} {:answer/id #uuid "d9fbb5f9-1876-576d-956d-164f993762da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\in [2,4]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325870} {:answer/id #uuid "e3d1017a-3133-56bf-ad84-e9bd0f77a8d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\in [2,6]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325