, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & -1\\le \\sin(x+90^{\\circ})\\le 1 \\\\  & \\frac{7}{3}\\ge - \\frac{7}{3}\\sin(x+90^{\\circ})\\ge - \\frac{7}{3} \\\\  & \\frac{73}{12}\\ge - \\frac{7}{3}\\sin(x+90^{\\circ})+\\frac{15}{4}\\ge \\frac{17}{12} \\\\  & \\frac{17}{12}\\le y\\le \\frac{73}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range is $y\\in [\\frac{17}{12},\\frac{73}{12}].$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531878 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5696c2d5-4e35-5ed3-a4a2-6fe9b158e461" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Range of a Transformed Sinusoidal Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "026d450b-1fc8-55c5-a3e4-c7ea05779d7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531859} {:answer/id #uuid "34a1288f-9e41-57a2-8601-0fc8e84d7ae6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531870} {:answer/id #uuid "39536aaf-4a33-57f0-a2ae-b08e6ad8c365" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531873} {:answer/id #uuid "c7ca28f7-3440-528e-b36e-9776d615005f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531912} {:answer/id #uuid "f381e07a-8f5e-5e4c-ba31-9a69e3132923" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531925}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39536aaf-4a33-57f0-a2ae-b08e6ad8c365" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531873} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4139737-cb8b-5107-b124-0a0b3dbd4c26" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531907}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4a8a1aef-2486-5547-9b46-00e8b9822b23" :question/problem "What is the minimum value of $f(x)=-3\\sin(2x+1)+2$?" :question/worked-solution "The range of $\\sin x$ is\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\sin x\\le 1.\n$$\n\nHorizontal shifts and stretches have no effect on the range. Therefore,\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\sin(2x+1)\\le 1.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $-3$ and then adding $2$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & -1\\le \\sin(2x+1)\\le 1 \\\\  & 3\\ge -3\\sin(2x+1)\\ge -3 \\\\  & 5\\ge -3\\sin(2x+1)+2\\ge -1 \\\\  & -1\\le f(x)\\le 5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the minimum value is $-1.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531882 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5696c2d5-4e35-5ed3-a4a2-6fe9b158e461" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Range of a Transformed Sinusoidal Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "058c4a02-5842-5f2f-b56c-8ffbb80c91a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\in [- \\frac{13}{3},- \\frac{7}{3}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531862} {:answer/id #uuid "21ca9ef2-6c80-542c-a8ae-e2e9771fbb05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\in [- \\frac{101}{6},\\frac{61}{6}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531865} {:answer/id #uuid "47bb1d33-4b81-5a51-84fd-d4dd865d6da1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\in [- \\frac{7}{6},\\frac{47}{6}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531877} {:answer/id #uuid "77ee29f0-d812-52a5-8b80-8da9d568e6d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\in [- \\frac{9}{2},\\frac{9}{2}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531886} {:answer/id #uuid "fcc26598-de2b-53ff-b631-30e455b08647" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\in [- \\frac{47}{6},\\frac{7}{6}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531926}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fcc26598-de2b-53ff-b631-30e455b08647" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\in [- \\frac{47}{6},\\frac{7}{6}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531926} :answer-field/id #uuid "7dcead1a-e49d-5054-9922-d19274e9f742" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531888}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "59021155-036e-5413-8fa8-78b4b038741c" :question/problem "What is the range of the function $y=- \\frac{9}{2}\\sin(3x+\\pi)-\\frac{10}{3}$?" :question/worked-solution "The range of $\\sin x$ is\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\sin x\\le 1.\n$$\n\nHorizontal shifts and stretches have no effect on the range. Therefore,\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\sin(3x+\\pi)\\le 1.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $- \\frac{9}{2}$ and then subtracting $\\frac{10}{3}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & -1\\le \\sin(3x+\\pi)\\le 1 \\\\  & \\frac{9}{2}\\ge - \\frac{9}{2}\\sin(3x+\\pi)\\ge - \\frac{9}{2} \\\\  & \\frac{7}{6}\\ge - \\frac{9}{2}\\sin(3x+\\pi)-\\frac{10}{3}\\ge - \\frac{47}{6} \\\\  & - \\frac{47}{6}\\le y\\le \\frac{7}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range is $y\\in [- \\frac{47}{6},\\frac{7}{6}].$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531883 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5696c2d5-4e35-5ed3-a4a2-6fe9b158e461" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Range of a Transformed Sinusoidal Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84192e5b-0f14-58bd-ab09-b0b511ae1bb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531891} {:answer/id #uuid "ac46931e-ea8a-5deb-bfff-7c978c5f4d90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531904} {:answer/id #uuid "af10505c-a700-52de-b365-10b62965e87d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531905} {:answer/id #uuid "b8156ff3-b442-5ccc-8182-da4ace6c6b95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531908} {:answer/id #uuid "d2f29f95-91be-5052-aaa0-5901cabfdfa2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531914}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ac46931e-ea8a-5deb-b