}{3},6].$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531910 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5696c2d5-4e35-5ed3-a4a2-6fe9b158e461" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Range of a Transformed Sinusoidal Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38cc2327-7b59-5809-bf47-5b90767993e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\in [-7,-5]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531872} {:answer/id #uuid "7ca2e692-22f3-5ae3-9dcd-9d930f9ec20a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\in [-14,2]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531887} {:answer/id #uuid "7e74b8ec-0eff-5cac-86a0-0b2d0707e64f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\in [2,10]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531889} {:answer/id #uuid "c4d758c6-063b-5b43-b04d-ecab4a9ec2ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\in [-4,4]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531911} {:answer/id #uuid "dd0c53a2-bb9a-55dd-b893-aa9e04bffd10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\in [-10,-2]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531918}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd0c53a2-bb9a-55dd-b893-aa9e04bffd10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\in [-10,-2]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531918} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea0396ba-5f56-58e3-a8d5-1e9cf69982b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531922}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bfa79656-9e84-52d8-a0b6-2b19c73026df" :question/problem "What is the range of the function $y=4\\cos(2x-3)-6$?" :question/worked-solution "The range of $\\cos x$ is\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\cos x\\le 1.\n$$\n\nHorizontal shifts and stretches have no effect on the range. Therefore,\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\cos(2x-3)\\le 1.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $4$ and then subtracting $6$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & -1\\le \\cos(2x-3)\\le 1 \\\\  & -4\\le 4\\cos(2x-3)\\le 4 \\\\  & -10\\le 4\\cos(2x-3)-6\\le -2 \\\\  & -10\\le y\\le -2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range is $y\\in [-10,-2].$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531915 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5696c2d5-4e35-5ed3-a4a2-6fe9b158e461" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Range of a Transformed Sinusoidal Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51fc8ff6-ff59-55b0-8e3d-ce5c027fc2b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531881} {:answer/id #uuid "8c5811c4-17b1-5d9c-967e-ca4d95873379" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{11}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531893} {:answer/id #uuid "97d8c43f-6d19-59e4-bc24-8a923371c9c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531894} {:answer/id #uuid "9cbc1339-2a31-5ebc-8993-d9ec3f4e630c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531897} {:answer/id #uuid "a7db53c0-c38d-59a5-90de-54209b3baa0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531901}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97d8c43f-6d19-59e4-bc24-8a923371c9c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531894} :answer-field/id #uuid "41904b8f-5499-5e65-8f16-1e206050837a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531875}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d54efe1e-4acd-544c-a88b-e2e33325c7bd" :question/problem "What is the minimum value of $f(x)=- \\frac{5}{2}\\cos(5x-2)-\\frac{11}{2}$?" :question/worked-solution "The range of $\\cos x$ is\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\cos x\\le 1.\n$$\n\nHorizontal shifts and stretches have no effect on the range. Therefore,\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\cos(5x-2)\\le 1.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $- \\frac{5}{2}$ and then subtracting $\\frac{11}{2}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & -1\\le \\cos(5x-2)\\le 1 \\\\  & \\frac{5}{2}\\ge - \\frac{5}{2}\\cos(5x-2)\\ge - \\frac{5}{2} \\\\  & -3\\ge - \\frac{5}{2}\\cos(5x-2)-\\frac{11}{2}\\ge -8 \\\\  & -8\\le f(x)\\le -3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the minimum value is $-8.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Range of a Transformed Sinusoidal Function"}]}
